Build succeeded. The fix addresses the timeout issue by properly handling EOF when no data has been read (returning NULL immediately), which allows the main loop to terminate correctly on empty input or end of file.

**What was failing:** The `read_line()` function had flawed EOF detection logic that caused infinite loops on certain inputs, particularly empty input or when reaching end of file without reading any characters.

**What I changed:** Simplified the EOF handling in `read_line()` - now returns NULL immediately if EOF is encountered with `len == 0`, otherwise breaks and returns whatever was read.

**Build command run:** `mkdir -p build && cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic -O2 src/new_grep/new_grep.c -o build/new_grep`

